11. Security rules for the backend
Session security

Secure, HttpOnly, SameSite cookies, session rotation and server-side session revocation.

Password security

Password hashing with Argon2id or equivalent, breached-password checks where feasible, and server-enforced policy.

Login protection

Rate limiting, progressive throttling, audit logs and generic errors that do not reveal whether an account exists.

Invitation and recovery tokens

Random single-use tokens, hashed at rest, expiring, invalidated after successful use.

RBAC enforcement

Every protected API endpoint checks authorization independently of frontend route guards.

Data protection

Minimal profile data, access logging, secure recovery processes and protection of student records.

